                <pb facs="0424" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg402"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p> NSC document 73/4, “The Position and Action of the United States With Respect to
                    Possible Further Soviet Moves in the Light of the Korean Situation,” August 25,
                    1950, printed in <ref target="frus:frus1950v01/pg_375">volume I, page 375</ref>,
                    recommended that in the event of an overt attack by organized Soviet military
                    forces against Greece or Turkey, the United States should provide accelerated
                    military assistance to either country and deploy <pb facs="0425" n="403"
                        xml:id="pg403"/> such United States forces to their support as could be made
                    available without jeopardizing United States national security.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
